<p>
  {dgettext(
    "help_ui",
    "RetroHexChat can be installed straight from the browser. It then gets its own icon and its own window, with no address bar — the same chat, reached the way any other app on the device is reached."
  )}
</p>
<.help_h4 icon={:icon_tab_control}>{dgettext("help_ui", "How to Install")}</.help_h4>
<ul>
  <li>
    {dgettext(
      "help_ui",
      "Desktop Chrome or Edge: an install icon appears at the right of the address bar, or use the browser menu's Install option"
    )}
  </li>
  <li>{dgettext("help_ui", "Android Chrome: menu, then Add to Home screen")}</li>
  <li>{dgettext("help_ui", "iPhone or iPad Safari: Share, then Add to Home Screen")}</li>
</ul>
<.help_h4 icon={:icon_lightbulb}>{dgettext("help_ui", "What Changes")}</.help_h4>
<ul>
  <li>
    {dgettext("help_ui", "Opening the icon lands you on the chat rather than the front page")}
  </li>
  <li>{dgettext("help_ui", "The window has no browser chrome")}</li>
  <li>
    {dgettext(
      "help_ui",
      "Nothing is stored offline: the chat needs the server, and an installed copy showing a stale screen would be worse than not opening at all"
    )}
  </li>
</ul>
<.help_h4 icon={:icon_warning}>{dgettext("help_ui", "This Is Not Self-Hosting")}</.help_h4>
<p>
  {dgettext(
    "help_ui",
    "Installing puts this chat on your device. Running your own server is a different thing entirely, and it has its own guide on the website."
  )}
</p>
<.help_h4 icon={:icon_link}>{dgettext("help_ui", "See Also")}</.help_h4>
<p>
  <.help_link topic="ui-overview">{dgettext("help_ui", "User Interface Overview")}</.help_link>
  ·
  <.help_link topic="feature-desktop-notifications">
    {dgettext("help_ui", "Desktop Notifications")}
  </.help_link>
</p>
